# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every pinned version in the workshop lives here and nowhere else.
# Docs and scripts both read from this file, so a refresh is one edit + one
# test run.
#
# Last validated: 2026-08-18 on Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS, amd64, t3.xlarge
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Host OS -----------------------------------------------------------------
UBUNTU_RELEASE="24.04"
JDK_VERSION="21"                      # PetClinic targets 17; builds clean on 21

# --- Kubernetes toolchain ----------------------------------------------------
MINIKUBE_VERSION="v1.38.1"
KUBECTL_VERSION="v1.36.3"             # PINNED. Never resolve stable.txt at install
                                      # time — two participants on different days
                                      # would get different clients.
K8S_VERSION="v1.35.1"                 # what minikube v1.38.1 provisions
MINIKUBE_SUBNET="192.168.49.0/24"
MINIKUBE_RUNTIME="docker"             # explicit: v1.39 flips the default to containerd

# --- Helm --------------------------------------------------------------------
HELM_VERSION="v4.2.4"                 # chart supports "Helm 3.9+ or Helm 4.x"
                                      # Installed from get.helm.sh, NOT the baltocdn
                                      # apt repo — that host now fails TLS validation.

# --- Splunk ------------------------------------------------------------------
SPLUNK_VERSION="10.4.2"
SPLUNK_BUILD_HASH="33c3bf42cd73"
SPLUNK_TGZ="splunk-${SPLUNK_VERSION}-${SPLUNK_BUILD_HASH}-linux-amd64.tgz"
# ~1.6 GB download (9.0.4.1 was ~600 MB) — call this out in prerequisites.

# --- OpenTelemetry -----------------------------------------------------------
OTEL_CHART_VERSION="0.158.0"
OTEL_CHART_REPO="https://signalfx.github.io/splunk-otel-collector-chart"
# AW1 no longer downloads splunk-otel-javaagent.jar by hand or bakes a
# -javaagent flag into a Dockerfile — it can't, once five of the six PetClinic
# services are pulled prebuilt images with no Dockerfile to edit. Instead the
# chart's own OpenTelemetry Operator (operator.enabled / instrumentation.enabled
# in values-aw1.yaml) injects the agent via an admission webhook, using
# whatever image chart 0.158.0's Instrumentation CRD defaults to
# (ghcr.io/signalfx/splunk-otel-java/splunk-otel-java:v2.30.0, as of this
# chart version) — not this variable. Nothing in the workshop reads
# SPLUNK_OTEL_JAVA_VERSION any more; kept only as a historical marker of the
# last version the old manual approach pinned, in case a future module still
# wants a hand-attached agent for contrast.
SPLUNK_OTEL_JAVA_VERSION="v2.30.2"

# --- Application -------------------------------------------------------------
# spring-petclinic-microservices — six Spring Boot services replacing the old
# single-pod spring-petclinic monolith. See AGENTS.md and the migration plan
# for why: it makes AW1's service map and AW2's APM/RUM sections real, and
# gives FW1 a real Kubernetes topology to run Cilium against.
PETCLINIC_MICROSVC_REPO="https://github.com/spring-petclinic/spring-petclinic-microservices.git"
PETCLINIC_MICROSVC_TAG="v3.2.0"        # NOT v3.4.1 — that release adds genai-service,
                                        # which needs an OPENAI_API_KEY. v3.2.0 is the
                                        # newest tag without it, same Java 17 / Spring
                                        # Boot 3.x runtime, identical gateway routing.
PETCLINIC_MICROSVC_BASE_IMAGE="eclipse-temurin:17-jre-noble"
# api-gateway's served index.html (the AngularJS SPA), inside the pulled
# image — confirmed live 2026-08-29, scripts/inject-rum-snippet.sh (AW2)
# relies on this exact path. Paketo buildpacks layout, not a plain jar's
# static/ root, which is why it isn't just /static/index.html. Re-check if
# PETCLINIC_MICROSVC_TAG ever moves to a release built on a different base
# image/buildpack.
PETCLINIC_API_GATEWAY_STATIC_PATH="/application/BOOT-INF/classes/static/index.html"
# Fully-qualified autoconfiguration class disabled via SPRING_AUTOCONFIGURE_EXCLUDE
# in instrumentation.spec.java.env (values-aw1.yaml onward) — confirmed live
# 2026-08-30 as the only fix (of three tried) that actually silences PetClinic's
# own bundled Zipkin auto-export, which otherwise floods every trace with
# failing localhost:9411 spans. Tied to this Spring Boot version's package
# layout, same as PETCLINIC_API_GATEWAY_STATIC_PATH above — re-check if
# PETCLINIC_MICROSVC_TAG ever moves to a release on a different Spring Boot
# major version.
PETCLINIC_ZIPKIN_AUTOCONFIG_CLASS="org.springframework.boot.actuate.autoconfigure.tracing.zipkin.ZipkinAutoConfiguration"
# A second, unrelated localhost source: every service's own application.yml
# (upstream source, all six — confirmed identical for customers-service,
# vets-service, api-gateway) imports config via
# spring.config.import: optional:configserver:${CONFIG_SERVER_URL:http://localhost:8888/}
# in its default profile. Setting this env var closes the placeholder, so the
# default profile's import resolves the same real address the docker
# profile's own hardcoded import already uses, instead of failing against
# localhost first. This is the literal env var name the ${...} placeholder
# reads — not a Spring relaxed-binding property name, so don't rename it to
# match spring.cloud.config.uri's usual SPRING_CLOUD_CONFIG_URI form; that
# was tried and confirmed to do nothing.
PETCLINIC_CONFIG_SERVER_URL_VAR="CONFIG_SERVER_URL"
PETCLINIC_MICROSVC_CONFIG_REPO="https://github.com/spring-petclinic/spring-petclinic-microservices-config"
# ^ Source of the six files baked into the ConfigMap in
# labs/manifests/petclinic-microservices.yml — copied by hand, not fetched at
# install time. Config Server's own default (a live git pull from this repo's
# `main` branch, on every restart) is disabled; see that manifest's header
# comment. Re-copy the files if you bump PETCLINIC_MICROSVC_TAG to a release
# with a materially different config shape — diff against upstream first.
PETCLINIC_MICROSVC_MINIMUM_VCPU=8      # Verified 2026-08-28: 4 vCPU / 16 GB drove
                                        # load average to 66 and the kubelet missed
                                        # its node-lease renewal — Kubernetes marked
                                        # the node NotReady and evicted every pod,
                                        # this application included. 8 vCPU / 32 GB
                                        # held stable through a 3-minute traffic soak
                                        # with the node Ready throughout. Below this,
                                        # do not proceed past FW1 §2.
CURL_IMAGE="curlimages/curl:8.21.0"    # init-container image gating every dependent
                                        # service on config-server's health endpoint

# --- Application (legacy single-pod monolith, retired after FW1 — AW1 no
#     longer builds against it as of the operator-based auto-instrumentation
#     rewrite; kept here until AW2's own rewrite reaches the same point) -----
PETCLINIC_REPO="https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-petclinic.git"
PETCLINIC_BRANCH="main"               # the old 'springboot3' branch is frozen upstream
PETCLINIC_BASE_IMAGE="eclipse-temurin:21-jre-noble"
# NOTE: never hardcode the built jar name. It moved 3.0.0 -> 4.0.0-SNAPSHOT.
# Detect it: JAR=$(ls -1 target/*.jar | grep -v 'sources\|javadoc\|original' | head -1)

# --- Load generation ---------------------------------------------------------
JMETER_VERSION="5.6.3"                # stock Apache; FW2's plan needs no plugins
JMETER_URL="https://archive.apache.org/dist/jmeter/binaries/apache-jmeter-${JMETER_VERSION}.tgz"
# AW2 RUM uses Playwright instead of the JMeter WebDriver plugin — see 04-advanced-2.

# FW2 §7 onward: the always-on in-cluster load generator. Official image, no
# Dockerfile — see labs/loadgen/playwright-loadgen.yaml. PIP version MUST match
# the image tag's own bundled-browser version exactly (confirmed live,
# 2026-09-02): a match reuses the image's pre-baked Chromium in seconds; a
# mismatch triggers Playwright's own browser download instead.
PLAYWRIGHT_LOADGEN_IMAGE="mcr.microsoft.com/playwright/python:v1.62.0-noble"
PLAYWRIGHT_LOADGEN_PIP_VERSION="1.62.0"

# --- Workshop identifiers ----------------------------------------------------
# WS_USER is per-participant. Everything namespaced by it so a shared Splunk or
# Observability org doesn't collide between attendees.
: "${WS_USER:=$(whoami)}"
CLUSTER_NAME="${WS_USER}-minikube-cluster"
# The Collector/operator/Instrumentation CR live in their own cluster-scoped
# namespace, NOT default — user-directed, 2026-08-31: infrastructure
# components shouldn't share default with anything else. NOT WS_USER-prefixed
# — every participant's own single-node minikube cluster only ever has one
# collector installation in it, so there's no shared surface for two
# participants' names to collide on (same reasoning as the six PetClinic
# Service names in labs/manifests/petclinic-microservices*.yml). Every
# `instrumentation.opentelemetry.io/inject-java` annotation value and every
# `helm upgrade`/`install` command needs this as `--namespace`.
OTEL_NAMESPACE="otel"
IDX_LOGS="k8s_ws_logs"
IDX_APP_LOGS="k8s_ws_petclinic_logs"
IDX_TRACES="k8s_ws_traces"
IDX_METRICS="k8s_ws_metrics"
IDX_APP_METRICS="k8s_ws_petclinic_metrics"

# CI tooling — pinned for the same reason everything else is: an unpinned
# upgrade should never be able to fail a build that changed nothing.
GITLEAKS_VERSION="8.30.1"
MKDOCS_MATERIAL_VERSION="9.7.7"

# --- Workshop dashboard app -------------------------------------------------
WORKSHOP_APP_VERSION="1.0.6"
